  "articleBody": "It's easy to make a few missteps when you're tackling a home restoration project, but don't worry, we can help you avoid them! One of the biggest mistakes people make is delaying documentation. It might seem like a small thing, but taking photos and notes of the damage early on is vital. This helps establish a clear picture of what happened and can be a lifesaver if there are any disputes later. Another common error? Starting cosmetic repairs before the underlying issue, like moisture or structural problems, is fully resolved. You definitely don't want to just paint over a water stain if the leak is still active; it'll just come back! Also, many folks forget to compare the damage against pre-incident records. Having photos or descriptions of your home before the damage occurred can be incredibly helpful for insurance or just ensuring everything is restored to its original state. Finally, not tracking the repair progress with a clear work order and cost breakdown can lead to headaches. You want to know exactly what's being done and what you're paying for at every step. At HH Remodeling LLC, we’re all about open communication and clear processes. We're here to help you avoid these pitfalls and make your restoration project go smoothly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
